  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/976d272c722f9714461afcb4b299f2ab03a50c7a introduced a check to cancel ongoing navigations \n\nAfter applying that change to Ladybird, I have later noticed that we have regressed on the test case of:\n\nhttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/url/javascript-urls.window.js\n\nWith our new results being:\n\n```\nHarness status: OK\n\nFound 6 tests\n\n3 Pass\n3 Fail\nPass\tjavascript: URL that fails to parse due to invalid host\nPass\tjavascript: URL that fails to parse due to invalid host and has a U+0009 in scheme\nPass\tjavascript: URL with extra slashes at the start\nFail\tjavascript: URL without an opaque path\nFail\tjavascript: URL containing a JavaScript string split over path and query\nFail\tjavascript: URL containing a JavaScript string split over path and query and has a U+000A in scheme\n```\n\nBased on the comment: https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12076#issuecomment-3756206523\n\nMy suspicion of the issue here is that at least Chromium (who is the only browser passing this test currently) only performs this check / cancelling in form submission, and not during anchor click activation handler.",
